      "dom_id": "question-68496",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Emma bought $2$ pounds of raisins for  $\\$4.80.$ What's the unit price per ounce?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ ounces in one pound.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert from pounds to ounces. There are $16$ ounces in each pound, so we multiply the number of pounds  by $16:$  \n\n$$\n2\\times 16=32\n$$\n\nSo, $2$ pounds is the same as $32$ ounces. Now, to find the unit price per ounce, we divide the total price by $32:$\n\n$$\n4.80÷32=0.15\n$$\n\nTherefore, the raisins cost $\\$0.15$ per ounce.",
