      "dom_id": "question-354928",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Emily filled a container with $48$ fluid ounces of juice and paid $\\$11.52$ for it. What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert from fluid ounces to cups. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we divide the number of fluid ounces by $8:$     \n\n$$\n48÷8=6\n$$\n\nSo, $48$ fluid ounces is the same as $6$ cups. Now, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $6:$ \n\n$$\n11.52÷6=1.92\n$$\n\nTherefore, the juice costs $\\$1.92$ per cup.",
